  "caption": "Quinn rolled an ankle at footy and planned a recovery party. The ankle was not impressed.\n\nAlcohol and smoking can slow tissue and bone repair. Smoking reduces blood flow and oxygen to healing tissue, and alcohol disrupts deep sleep and can blunt strength gains. The effects are mostly about heavy or frequent use, not a single drink.\n\nWhat often helps: go easy on alcohol in the first few days after an injury, keep it moderate during rehab, ask your GP about support to quit smoking (especially before planned surgery), and back the basics: sleep, protein and staying active.\n\nIf pain or swelling isn't settling, get it checked.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
